  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong dark editorial composition, consistent cyan/red accents, crisp card system, and clear headline-to-metric hierarchy across viewports. However, much supporting copy and chart/table labeling is extremely small and low-contrast—especially on mobile—making the polished surface feel compressed rather than confidently readable. The mobile ablation table becomes dense stacked micro-cards, while the global header visibly clips its navigation at tablet/mobile and drops the brand wordmark and red-mode action on mobile, weakening hierarchy and finish.",
